Input: bound N
Output: (verified, counterexamples)

is_prime ← sieve(N)
counterexamples ← []
for n = 4, 6, ..., N:
    found ← false
    for p = 2 to n/2:
        if is_prime[p] and is_prime[n-p]:
            found ← true; break
    if not found:
        counterexamples.append(n)
return (len(counterexamples) = 0, counterexamples)

Complexity: O(N²/log²N) time, O(N) space

